From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office-wp14 <wp14@office.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:41:52 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 41/42] ui-egui: the interface language sets the number locale
 of typed input and cell text

Language::num_locale (Ru, Uz-Latn, Uz-Cyrl; every other language, Spanish included, stays en-US), with
GRIDCRAFT_NUM_LOCALE as the override. Once per frame it goes to Session.prefs and the egui context.
The grid shows cells with format_in; the editor opens a number or date in the locale's typing form
(12.10.2026, 3500000,5) and the commit turns what was typed back into en-US input text with
to_invariant, so the engine, validation, the journal and macros only see en-US. 12.10.2026 is 12 October
in ru and uz; 1.234 stays text; a text-formatted cell keeps what was typed. Ctrl+; and Ctrl+' insert
the locale's short date.

Russian and Uzbek formulas are entered with ; and a decimal comma (FormulaLocale::DecimalComma); the stored formula and the xlsx keep SUM(1,2).
